%I A399298 #18 Sep 02 2026 19:56:43
%S A399298 1,2,3,6,5,6,7,14,9,10,25,18,13,14,23,30,17,30,41,30,57,50,23,58,25,
%T A399298 26,27,42,121,46,65,62,75,66,59,114,37,162,63,102,85,114,43,150,77,90,
%U A399298 139,202,49,50,83,78,53,102,317,146,123,242,121,138,125,258,207
%N A399298 Number of cycles of the discrete Arnold cat map on an n X n array.
%C A399298 The discrete Arnold cat map is the permutation (x,y) -> (2*x+y,x+y) mod n of (Z/nZ)^2. This convention is conjugate by coordinate swap to the map used in A281230. Since its determinant is 1, every component of its functional graph is a cycle.
%C A399298 A281230(n) is the order of the same permutation, equivalently the LCM of its cycle lengths. The present sequence counts the cycles themselves. These invariants differ; for n=3 the cycle lengths are 1,4,4, so a(3)=3 whereas A281230(3)=4.
%H A399298 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A399298/b399298.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..100</a>
%H A399298 Fei Chen, Kwok-Wo Wong, Xiaofeng Liao, and Tao Xiang, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tcs.2014.08.002">Period distribution of generalized discrete Arnold cat map</a>, Theoretical Computer Science, 552 (2014), 13-25.
%H A399298 Freeman J. Dyson and Harold Falk, <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2324989">Period of a Discrete Cat Mapping</a>, American Mathematical Monthly, 99 (1992), 603-614.
%H A399298 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A399298/a399298.cpp.txt">C++ program for computing the sequence</a>.
%H A399298 Chengqing Li, Kai Tan, Bingbing Feng, and Jinhu Lü, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.07905">The Graph Structure of the Generalized Discrete Arnold's Cat Map</a>, arXiv:1712.07905 [nlin.CD], 2017-2019.
%H A399298 Joe Nance, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.2984">Periods of the discretized Arnold Cat Map and its extension to n dimensions</a>, arXiv:1111.2984 [math.DS], 2011.
%H A399298 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arnold%27s_cat_map">Arnold's cat map</a>.
%F A399298 a(n) = (1/T(n)) * Sum_{k=0..T(n)-1} b(n,k) where b(n,0) = n^2, b(n,k) = gcd(n,L(k))^2 for odd k, and b(n,k) = gcd(n,F(k)) * gcd(n,5*F(k)) for positive even k with T(n) = A281230(n), F(k) = A000045(k), and L(k) = A000032(k).
%e A399298 For n=3 the three cycles have lengths 1,4,4; hence a(3)=3. Their LCM is A281230(3)=4.
